The live integration milestone remains `R0i`. Elite/headless actor packets are
completed predecessor work. The latest event-card functional checkpoint is
`b2ae0dd`: generic mechanics plus three exact native event rows, not automatic
all-event support. Next is authoritative generic interaction discovery/admission
in a reviewed successor; do not default to adding Brain/Zen rows. Fourteen
successor trees are frozen. No new event-card release or live setup is ready.
A complete autonomous run and target-game fidelity remain unclaimed.

Key invariants:

- keep structured observations separate from RL encoding
- keep stable enemy slots in multi-enemy combat
- keep action masks aligned with action encoding
- keep reward shaping oriented toward winning with more HP left
- maintain Python `3.10+` compatibility
